ST: drm/i915/gen9: Removed byte swapping for csr firmware  This patch contains the changes to remove the byte swapping logic introduced with old dmc firmware. While debugging PC10 entry issue for skylake found with latest dmc firmware version 1.18 without byte swapping dmc is working fine and able to enter PC10.  v1: Initial version.  v2: Corrected firmware size during memcpy(). (Suggested by Sunil)  Cc: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@intel.com&gt; Cc: Damien Lespiau &lt;damien.lespiau@intel.com&gt; Cc: Imre Deak &lt;imre.deak@intel.com&gt; Cc: Sunil Kamath &lt;sunil.kamath@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Animesh Manna &lt;animesh.manna@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Vathsala Nagaraju &lt;vathsala.nagaraju@intel.com&gt; (am from http://lists.freedesktop.org/archives/intel-gfx/2015-August/072871.html) Signed-off-by: Marc Herbert &lt;marc.herbert@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43454 TEST=with the whole series applied, and TEST=without a valid DMC/CSR firmware file in /lib/firmware/i915/: no change. TEST=with a valid DMC/CSR firmware in place: logs stop being continuously  flooded with WARNING intel_csr.c:473 assert_csr_loaded+0x31/0xc2()  Change-Id: I20f510e26b0a65103c8312ad2f91259d4ac2a670 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/290476 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Philip Hanson &lt;philip.hanson@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Joe Konno &lt;joe.konno@linux.intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="290476" owner_email="marc.herbert@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/76/290476/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I456d86bcb39c9261b8d5910f576d30fa26d3466c" commit="3dae793dd448e8d6015dbac51ca8c7c7687704e5" commit_message="camera_fixture: do not force new IP when getting parameter file  In ChromeOS factory, the device should get a new IP once it's connected to the network. Do not force a new IP when preparing network.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:42437 TEST=manually  Change-Id: I456d86bcb39c9261b8d5910f576d30fa26d3466c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305900 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305900" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/00/305900/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6ab344b17e7da103311e384c3e57b98e365f0179" commit="1c5c865e42280c0f05501fcb373a13d1fd612e87" commit_message="graphics_dEQP: unsupported GPU -&gt; TestNAError.  We want to keep track of these GPUs, in particular in preparation of moving graphics_dEQP into bvt-cq. And DEPENDENCIES don't work as they should. (Might still be worth adding DEPENDENCIES in addition to avoid lab overhead though.)  BUG=chromium:510208 TEST=None.  Change-Id: I6ab344b17e7da103311e384c3e57b98e365f0179 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305715 Commit-Ready: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305715" owner_email="ihf@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/15/305715/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic199701ab5f8125f08cffd931a30b01c641ee564" commit="5c3723a495f3dc0635e4af499bea494646241ef2" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: mt8173-oak: access EC with HW SPI  Since SW SPI is too slow to make ectool command fail sometimes. Instead of SW SPI, we access EC with HW SPI.  Signed-off-by: YH Huang &lt;yh.huang@mediatek.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:42023 TEST=run a simple stress test with the following setting   1. run several busy loop of power_supply_info for talking to EC via      hardware SPI   2. prepare another EC image and execute flashrom -p ec /tmp/ec.bin   3. There should not be any &quot;SPI rx bad data&quot; on EC console      nor &quot;spi32766.0: EC failed to respond in time&quot; printed in      /var/log/messages  Change-Id: Ic199701ab5f8125f08cffd931a30b01c641ee564 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303282 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303282" owner_email="yh.huang@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/82/303282/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I7bca535d6a86e7bd314ce6569ce76b260afbf18f" commit="0a0e9c5d9789291c27083907ac1b8adce63707db" commit_message="FIXUP: CHROMIUM: v4l2-mem2mem: allow reqbufs(0) with &quot;in use&quot; MMAP buffers  &quot;CHROMIUM: v4l2-mem2mem: allow reqbufs(0) with &quot;in use&quot; MMAP buffers&quot; being a port from 3.8 missed a mutex_lock() call that wasn't there in 3.8, but is present in newer versions of the kernel. Add it back.  Signed-off-by: Pawel Osciak &lt;posciak@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=None TEST=vdatest  Change-Id: I7bca535d6a86e7bd314ce6569ce76b260afbf18f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305860 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Pawel Osciak &lt;posciak@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurt